§ `s 4 -- time`

#ASSERT `the court may extend the period` `a later-discovered will or codicil substantially changing the disposition` TRUE
#ASSERT `the court may extend the period` `an undetermined question about an interest in the estate` TRUE
#ASSERT `the court may extend the period` `other circumstances affecting administration or distribution` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the court may extend the period` `none of the listed reasons` TRUE

#ASSERT `the application is in time` 3 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the application is in time` 7 FALSE
#ASSERT `the application is in time` 18 TRUE

#ASSERT `the grant starts the six months` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the grant starts the six months` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the grant starts the six months` TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 2, 3(3), 3(4), 5(2) -- amounts`

#ASSERT `the net estate` 1000000 20000 80000 0 EQUALS 900000

#ASSERT `a lump sum may be ordered` 40000
#ASSERT `a lump sum may be ordered` 50000
#ASSERT NOT `a lump sum may be ordered` 50001

#ASSERT `the periodical payments are within the income cap` 20000 30000 36000
#ASSERT NOT `the periodical payments are within the income cap` 20000 40000 36000

#ASSERT `the largest part that may be set aside` 12000 4 EQUALS 300000

§ `s 3(2) -- when payments must end`

#ASSERT NOT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `widow-of-60` `nothing-yet`
#ASSERT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `widow-of-60` `married`
#ASSERT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `widow-of-60` `died`
#ASSERT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `unmarried-daughter-of-45` `married`
#ASSERT NOT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `unmarried-disabled-daughter` `married`
#ASSERT NOT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `unmarried-disabled-daughter` `disability-ended`
#ASSERT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `unmarried-disabled-daughter` `married-and-disability-ended`
#ASSERT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `son-of-17` `turned-21`
#ASSERT NOT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `disabled-son-of-35` `turned-21`
#ASSERT `the latest end of the payments has been reached` `disabled-son-of-35` `disability-ended`

§ `s 6 -- variation`

#ASSERT `a late order may be made under section 6` `a material fact was not disclosed` TRUE
#ASSERT `a late order may be made under section 6` `a substantial change in the circumstances of the dependant or a beneficiary` TRUE
#ASSERT `a late order may be made under section 6` `provision for another dependant` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a late order may be made under section 6` `none of the listed grounds` TRUE

#ASSERT `may apply to vary under section 6(1)(a)` `a dependant`
#ASSERT `may apply to vary under section 6(1)(a)` `the trustees of the property`
#ASSERT `may apply to vary under section 6(1)(a)` `a beneficiary of the property`
#ASSERT NOT `may apply to vary under section 6(1)(a)` `a creditor of the estate`

